      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that. i've been reading some stuff and it seems like a lot of the 'privacy' concerns are basically just things that can be fixed with better encryption or better laws, right? like, if we just regulate how the data is used, doesn't the massive boost in public safety and transit efficiency pretty much make the tech a net positive for the city? wouldn't the benefits just outweigh the risks once the legal stuff is settled?",
